      "id": 1,
      "text": "The Glen Ferris Inn, built in 1810, was the first permanent building constructed in the village.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glen_Ferris%2C_West_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Famous guests at the Glen Ferris Inn included Andrew Jackson, Henry Clay, and naturalist John James Audubon.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glen_Ferris%2C_West_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Remnants of Camp Reynolds, a Union Army camp and gun embankment from the Civil War, lie across from the inn.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glen_Ferris%2C_West_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Glen Ferris is situated adjacent to the Kanawha Falls and is roughly a mile and a half in length.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glen_Ferris%2C_West_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Brick remains of a small hydroelectric plant purchased by Union Carbide in 1917 are still visible on the riverbank.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glen_Ferris%2C_West_Virginia"
    },
    {
